//
// ⚠ `uLut1.a` WAS A CONSTANT 255, which is the only reason this is free: the grid is already built,
// already uploaded and already sampled by both water shaders, so shelter costs one write per tile
// here and one swizzle there rather than a second texture and a second upload.
//
// ⚠ AND THE WIND IS IN THE CACHE KEY, QUANTISED. Shelter is the distance to land UPWIND, so it is a
// function of the wind as well as of the ground — but the wind turns continuously and this grid is
// rebuilt only when the window recentres, so keying on the raw bearing would rebuild it every
// frame. Sixteen sectors is 22.5 degrees, which the weather takes minutes to cross.
