// `marks` is the NAV_MARKS switch (see there), and it reaches exactly ONE branch of this function:
// the off-screen chevron. A contact you can see is a real aeroplane in the world and is drawn either
// way — what it turns off is the arrow pinned to the edge of the frame for one you cannot.
//
// ⚠ THE `continue` IS NOT INSIDE THE MARK. An off-screen contact has no model to draw, so the branch
// still has to skip the rest of the loop body whether or not it drew a chevron; guarding the whole
