    // line PER FACE, drawn along whichever edge the builder happened to emit first. On a fixed-wing
    // hull that is a few dozen big ring panels and it reads as a shine down the crown, which is what
    // it was written for. On anything built out of many small quads it is a bright line every few
    // pixels, running along the triangulation rather than along the form — and because a triangulated
    // band alternates its first edge, they cross. Reported as "the weave pattern that exists for some
    // reason", measured at several hundred flicks on one boat, and invisible on the same model in
    // satin or matte, which is what made it look like a geometry bug rather than a finish.
    //
    // The bar is the MODEL's own projected size rather than a pixel count, so it is the same
