// "boring sign that doesn't look real" report, and it is the same shape of finding `signFontOf`
// was written for one layer along: the city had one answer where a real street has several.
//
// A real street's signs differ in KIND before they differ in colour. Four here, and each is a
// thing the other three physically cannot be:
//   · `tube`    — the neon box that used to be the only answer. Dark board, glass round the edge.
//   · `box`     — a backlit lightbox: the FACE is the light and the letters are the dark. It is
//                 the commonest shopfront sign there is and the city had none of it.
//   · `applied` — a plain board lit only by a trough in its own sill, throwing up at letters that
//                 are bolted on. The name is the only thing burning.
//   · `painted` — paint, and nothing emits at all.
