// ── A BERTH: ONE CLOCK AND ONE SET OF NUMBERS, WITH TWO READERS EACH ───────────────────────────
//
// A ship-to-shore gantry and the hull it is working are the same machine seen from two ends, and
// they are drawn by two different things: the crane is a `building_type` arm and the freighter is
// a `mark`. Everything they have to agree about therefore lives HERE, once — how far off the quay
// a hull lies, how wide it is, how high its weather deck is, how tall a container is, and WHEN a
