// and consecutive ships are stacked differently. Six, because a stack of one colour is a wall and
// a stack of every colour is bunting.
// ⚠ THIS IS THE WHOLE OF THE HANDOVER. The crane paints the box on its spreader with it and the
// hull paints the box that arrives with it, and neither can see the other — so the colour that
// swings out over the water is the colour that appears on her deck because both asked one function
// the same question, not because anything was passed between them.
// ⚠ AND NO TWO BOXES IN A ROW ARE THE SAME COLOUR, which is not decoration. The colour is the only
// thing tying the container on the spreader to the one that arrives on her deck, and a plain hash
// hands you a run of three the same about one lift in six — at which point you are watching a box
// go out and a box of the same colour appear, which is what the whole thing looked like before any
