// the berth beside it — an arm is handed its own tile and nothing else — so the only thing the two
// can share is the wall clock. Seeding it per tile would give the gantry and the hull two different
// answers to "is there a ship alongside", and the visible result is a crane working over open water
// while a ship sits a hundred feet away doing nothing.
//
// The cost is real and small: a second port anywhere in the world runs its ships in step with this
