  // due north is -π/2. The turn off it is what keeps him from addressing the plinth's own corner:
  // twelve degrees is enough to read as a three-quarter pose from the square without looking as
  // though the casting was bolted down crooked. The seed survives as a couple of degrees of
  // jitter — a hand-poured bronze is not machined square to its footing — and is world-stable.
  //
  // ⚠ AND THE CATCH HANGS IN FRONT OF HIM RATHER THAN OUT TO ONE SIDE. The first pose swung the
