  // that bound the park; what it actually does is separate them, so from three of the four
  // approaches you get a man and, a little way off, a fish. A monument is read as a SILHOUETTE,
  // and two shapes with sky between them are two objects. Everything the tackle does happens in
  // front of his chest now — he still looks out to sea over the top of it, and from any approach
